  "worked_solution": "The explicit formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence (in function notation) is\n\n$$\nf(n)=f(1)+(n-1)d,\\,n\\ge 1,\n$$\n\nso we need to determine the first term $f(1)$ and the common difference $d.$\n\nWe are given that the first term is $f(1)=-1,$ and we can use the recursive rule to compute the second term, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2) & =f(1)-7 \\\\  & =-1-7 \\\\  & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the first and second terms, we can compute the common difference:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =f(2)-f(1) \\\\  & =-8-(-1) \\\\  & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $f(1)=-1$ and $d=-7$ into the formula for the $n$th term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(n) & =f(1)+(n-1)d \\\\  & =-1+(n-1)(-7) \\\\  & =-1-7n+7 \\\\  & =-7n+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the formula for the $n$th term is\n\n$$\nf(n)=-7n+6,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$",
